# CTF-02 actual native build and PE reader source

This is a bounded adaptation of the existing CTF-01 production 84-line reader
at `.runtime/porting/CTF-01/production-independent-native-build-review-01/review_build.py`.
The original is preserved byte-for-byte in `before/review_build.py`. No existing
reader, build, PE report, binary or canonical source is modified.

Root will supply the actual build manifest and choose the actual lane:

```text
python -X utf8 -B <held review_build.py> --lane unit|production --build <actual-manifest-path>#<actual-sha256> --output-dir <fresh-output-directory>
```

The reader accepts no future build identity or successful outcome in advance.
Its literal build schemas are `ctf02-native-build.v1` for unit and
`ctf02-production-native-build.v1` for production. The actual manifest must
declare target `ctf02_unit_helper` or `ctf02_production_helper` respectively,
and status `pass-actual-3TU-link-and-preservation`.

The existing configure/compile/derivation receipt checks, full stream byte
bindings, source identity checks, preserved provider assertion and strict
retained-runtime PE inspection mechanism are unchanged. The selected source
count changes from seven to eight; the real CTF-02 targets each compile three
translation units. The combined configuration retains all 667 previous rows
and adds six, requiring 673 total. Core registration/present/absent counts
remain 643/631/12, and the original Construction object must not be selected.
The actual provider text must identify the inherited derived Construction TU.

The protection count changes from 26 to 28 to include the actual CTF-01
production linked original and its retained derivative. Root's actual build
preservation records remain the authority for the complete protected identity
set and unchanged core object facts. No new retention or proof stage is added.

At future authorized execution the existing PE primitive reads the actual
original and derived binaries, checks exact retained runtime sections and
directories, and requires its maps to equal the actual derivation maps.
This source-preparation task did not read either binary or actual build/PE
outputs, and did not import or run the primitive or this reader.

Output files are the same three PE maps and `review.json`. Report schemas are
`ctf02-independent-build-PE-review.v1` and
`ctf02-production-independent-build-PE-review.v1`, with unchanged status
`pass-exact-retained-PE-runtime-and-actual-build-identity`. Report fields retain
build/binary/derivation/source identities and add the selected lane/target.
Stdout remains exactly the compact `{review,status}` binding. Root's real
recorder will capture that command, its source and streams; the reader does
not claim it authored the Root build manifest.

This package is source-ready, not a built or executed review. Root must fully
read it and obtain the normal other-author source peer before actual use.
No engine, formatter, compiler, Cargo, Git, scientific result or weather file
was used. This is the existing build/PE review mechanism, not a new framework.
CTF-02 Original data integrity, element comparisons and integration gates
remain separate actual work; no numerical PASS is claimed by this source.
